The cell 'span differing from the document by a line break / value the whole of the span' specifies that the span is present in the document but differs by a line break, and the value is identical to the span. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [6ab8417a77f3b613]. Read as written, "no relaxation" implies that a span containing a line break where the document does not (or vice versa) is not considered to occur in the document, which would lead to a verdict of SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT. In the rewritten text, I change the span to match the document character for character. The rule then implies a verdict of GROUNDED (since the value remains identical to the span). Thus, the verdict moves.